WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.910
One outline figure.

2
00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:04.960
Watch it closely,
because it never changes.

3
00:00:05.010 --> 00:00:07.150
Caption one: slim.

4
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.000
The audience nods along.

5
00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.230
Caption two: skinny.

6
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.670
Caption three: scrawny.

7
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.030
Each time, the faces change.

8
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:20.130
Same body, same outline,
three different reactions.

9
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:22.470
So where does each verdict come from?

10
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.320
In this mission, you'll
check the dictionary first.

11
00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.120
Do slim, skinny and scrawny
really mean different things?

12
00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.330
You'll test verbs and nouns too.

13
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:33.210
A cottage, or a shack?

14
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:35.660
Puts down a cup, or slaps it?

15
00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:40.660
And you'll zoom in on single words,
in a travel article and in Dickens.

16
00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: explain why the same
body gets three different verdicts.
